# P5 reproducibility artifact — .gitignore
#
# NOTE: the frozen captures under data/raw/ and data/frozen/ are the reproducibility
# RECORD and are INTENTIONALLY TRACKED (~73 MB total). Do not add them here — the
# Zenodo deposit and any GitHub->Zenodo release must include them so `reproduce.sh`
# can verify and regenerate the results offline.

# secrets / keys — never commit
*.env
*.env.*
keys.env.txt
*.pem
**/API Keys/

# python virtualenv + caches
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store

# transient run logs (not needed to reproduce)
logs/*.log

# scratch temp
*.tmp
results/_preview_p1.png

# LaTeX build artifacts (keep .tex, .bib, .cls, .bst, .bbl, .pdf)
results/_*.png

# intermediates from Word (.docx) generation — not part of the source

# SSRN preprint — distributed separately, not part of the repo
ssrn/
# Generated deliverables live in paper/out/; sources in paper/src/; build scripts in
# paper/tools/. One directory per role, so nothing generated sits beside a source.
paper/src/*.aux
paper/src/*.log
paper/src/*.out
paper/src/*.blg
paper/src/*.abs
paper/src/*.fls
paper/src/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/src/manuscript_tracked.tex
paper/src/Figure_*.pdf
paper/tools/*.log

# LaTeX writes this when it tries to generate a font it cannot find (rsfs10, requested
# by the journal class but never used in the output). It is regenerated on every build,
# so tracking it made the tree dirty after each run.
paper/out/missfont.log
